# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Placement Day Simulator — environment
# Copy to .env.local (git-ignored). Everything is optional; each feature turns
# on when its key exists. Check what the server sees at GET /api/health.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── TIER 1: THE BRAIN (one key is enough) ────────────────────────────────────
# Groq is the recommended free start: sub-second interviewer turns, AND it
# unlocks cloud speech-to-text (Whisper) and a text-to-speech voice (Orpheus)
# with the same key. Get one at https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b         # default; the server auto-switches to a model your account
# GROQ_FALLBACK_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b # actually has if this one is missing (see /api/health)
#
# Token budget. Groq's free tier gives EVERY model its own 8,000 tokens/minute
# bucket, and one interviewer turn costs ~2,000-2,700 (measured). Two things
# keep the interviewer on its own bucket:
# GROQ_BACKGROUND_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.6-27b # scoring, guidance, resume, GD run here,
#                                        # not on the interviewer's model
#                                        # (LLM_BACKGROUND_MODEL for other backends)
# LLM_SPECULATE=0                        # mid-answer speculative pre-fetch: on for
#                                        # unmetered brains, OFF on Groq by default
#                                        # (it doubles token spend). 1 forces on.
# The Groq Orpheus VOICE needs a one-time terms acceptance by the org admin:
#   https://console.groq.com/playground?model=canopylabs%2Forpheus-v1-english
# Until then the app speaks with the on-device/system voice (never silent).

# Alternatives — the first key found wins unless LLM_PROVIDER says otherwise:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...                  # OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# GEMINI_API_KEY=...                     # GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=...                 # OPENROUTER_MODEL=meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1 # any OpenAI-compatible server (Ollama, vLLM…)
# LLM_API_KEY=...                        # + LLM_MODEL=...   (use LLM_PROVIDER=custom)

# Force a backend: groq | openai | gemini | openrouter | custom | claude-cli (dev) | mock
# LLM_PROVIDER=groq
# LLM_MOCK_CHAOS=1                       # dev only: make the mock brain fail 1 in 17 calls

# ── TIER 2: THE VOICE (streamed, sentence by sentence) ───────────────────────
# Best first. With NONE of these the app still speaks (on-device Kokoro voice,
# then the browser's system voice).
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=...                 # ELEVENLABS_MODEL=eleven_flash_v2_5  ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=...
# OPENAI_API_KEY (above) also unlocks    # OPENAI_TTS_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini-tts    OPENAI_TTS_VOICE=marin
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=...                   # DEEPGRAM_TTS_VOICE=aura-2-thalia-en
# GROQ_API_KEY (above) also unlocks      # GROQ_TTS_MODEL=canopylabs/orpheus-v1-english  GROQ_TTS_VOICE=hannah
# GEMINI_API_KEY (above) also unlocks    # GEMINI_TTS_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts GEMINI_TTS_VOICE=Aoede
# Pick one explicitly: elevenlabs | openai | deepgram | groq | gemini
# TTS_PROVIDER=elevenlabs

# Local studio voice (Chatterbox-TTS-Server, optional, dev machines).
# github.com/devnen/Chatterbox-TTS-Server — the PREFERRED engine when reachable:
# unmetered, studio voices, and the only one that performs paralinguistic tags
# ([laugh] [chuckle] [sigh] [gasp] [cough] [sniff] [groan] [shush]
# [clear throat]). Run the Turbo engine for those tags and for the lowest
# latency — set model.repo_id: "chatterbox-turbo" in that server's config.yaml,
# or switch it live in its Web UI engine dropdown.
# CHATTERBOX_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8004
# CHATTERBOX_VOICE=Emily.wav
#
# Generation tuning. The defaults are chosen for a STEADY interviewer rather
# than an expressive narrator — a voice that shifts character between the two
# halves of an answer is what "the interviewer has multiple voices" sounds like.
# CHATTERBOX_SEED=8675309       # fixed, non-zero -> deterministic sampling per
#                               # persona. 0 = the server's random behaviour,
#                               # which re-rolls the voice on every request.
# CHATTERBOX_TEMPERATURE=0.7    # 0.0-1.5. Lower = steadier and faster.
# CHATTERBOX_EXAGGERATION=0.5   # 0.0-2.0. Ignored by the Turbo engine.
# CHATTERBOX_CFG_WEIGHT=0.5     # 0.0-2.0. Ignored by the Turbo engine.
# CHATTERBOX_SPEED=1.0          # 0.25-4.0 playback rate.
# CHATTERBOX_CHUNK_SIZE=50      # 50-500. Chatterbox renders a whole chunk in
#                               # ONE forward pass, so this IS the
#                               # time-to-first-audio. 50 is the minimum.

# ── TIER 3: HEARING (speech-to-text) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Chrome's built-in recognizer is free and needs nothing. For every other
# browser (and better accuracy) the server transcribes VAD-cut utterances via
# the first of: GROQ_API_KEY (Whisper turbo) → OPENAI_API_KEY → DEEPGRAM_API_KEY
# STT_PROVIDER=groq                      # groq | openai | deepgram
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY also enables TRUE live streaming recognition in the browser
# (interim words as you speak) through a short-lived token. Disable with:
# DEEPGRAM_LIVE=0
# NEXT_PUBLIC_STT_LANG=en-IN             # Chrome recognizer language

# ── TIER 4: PRODUCTION PLATFORM ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED in production (NODE_ENV=production refuses to boot without it):
# AUTH_JWT_SECRET=                        # `openssl rand -hex 32`

# Accounts + server-side history (MongoDB / Atlas). Without it: guest mode,
# history stays in the browser. Required for sign-up on serverless hosts.
# MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://user:pass@cluster.mongodb.net/pds
# MONGODB_DB=pds
# PDS_ALLOW_FILE_USERS=1                  # single long-lived server only: keep .data/users.json in prod

# Cross-instance rate limiting (Upstash Redis REST). Without it: in-memory
# buckets per instance (fine on one server, weak on serverless).
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://...upstash.io
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=...

# Google sign-in (next-auth v5) — optional secondary provider; all three needed.
# AUTH_SECRET=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_ID=
# AUTH_GOOGLE_SECRET=
# AUTH_URL=https://your-deploy.example

# Long-term candidate memory across sessions (https://supermemory.ai) — optional.
# SUPERMEMORY_API_KEY=

# Public URL (OpenRouter attribution, absolute links) — optional.
# APP_URL=https://your-deploy.example

# Feature flags
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GD_ENABLED=0               # hide the Group Discussion room

# Development only: make this fraction of LLM calls fail as a 429 so the fallback
# chain can be exercised in a real session. Ignored in production.
# LLM_CHAOS_429=0.5
